WEBVTT

00:11.990 --> 00:13.110
I'm sorry!

00:16.440 --> 00:19.120
Did something happen at school?

00:19.120 --> 00:21.160
Does it have something to do with basketball?

00:21.490 --> 00:23.430
Did things not go well again?

00:23.430 --> 00:25.720
No, that's not it.

00:25.720 --> 00:29.000
I'm getting along well with everyone, so don't worry.

00:38.100 --> 00:41.430
Don't give up and do your best

00:41.430 --> 00:44.810
Try your luck and fight! Chin-up!

00:44.810 --> 00:47.860
I know perfectly

00:47.860 --> 00:51.530
How weak a person is on their own

00:51.730 --> 00:54.700
Things that are on the verge of being lost

00:54.700 --> 00:58.370
I hold them close to my chest

00:58.370 --> 01:01.330
Your gentle words

01:01.330 --> 01:05.290
Caress my cheeks

01:05.290 --> 01:08.330
The irritation that has been building up

01:08.330 --> 01:11.130
From wanting to reach the goal

01:11.130 --> 01:15.300
My heart that almost wants to burst out crying

01:15.300 --> 01:18.890
The place that warms it up

01:18.890 --> 01:21.810
Even if we have to go through the pain

01:21.810 --> 01:25.310
We have to protect this

01:25.310 --> 01:26.770
We're unripe fighters!

01:26.770 --> 01:28.690
We won't lose now

01:28.690 --> 01:32.070
We will raise our small hands up in the air

01:32.070 --> 01:35.490
Take in that vital power, embrace it

01:35.490 --> 01:38.950
Then release it towards the sky!

01:38.950 --> 01:40.490
The courage that cannot be stopped

01:40.490 --> 01:42.330
Tomorrow we'll jump and shoot!

01:42.330 --> 01:45.250
I will pass the ball to you

01:45.250 --> 01:49.540
The memories that are awoken by our calls

01:49.540 --> 01:53.090
Game

01:49.540 --> 01:53.090
Will move the game along

02:01.680 --> 02:07.560
The Small Girl's Wish

02:01.740 --> 02:04.190
Was it you guys who put that note in my locker?

02:04.190 --> 02:07.140
Hey, you better stop coaching the girls' basketball club now.

02:07.140 --> 02:08.060
Otherwise...

02:08.350 --> 02:11.180
Regardless, my coaching ends today.

02:14.490 --> 02:15.150
Then...

02:15.450 --> 02:17.860
Well, I only promised three days.

02:17.860 --> 02:19.910
I guess we were just overreacting.

02:19.910 --> 02:22.220
Gosh, Takenaka, you gave us such a shock.

02:22.220 --> 02:26.890
But Maho sounded really confident when she said that they had an amazing new coach.

02:26.890 --> 02:28.580
And that they'd definitely win the match.

02:28.900 --> 02:29.500
"Match"?

02:29.850 --> 02:33.380
It's a match between the guys' basketball club and the girls' basketball club.

02:33.380 --> 02:35.210
That's the reason you came to coach, right?

02:35.210 --> 02:37.830
No, I never heard anything about that...

02:40.100 --> 02:43.470
Well, since your coaching ends today, we might as well tell you.

02:43.470 --> 02:46.020
We're having a match next Sunday.

02:46.300 --> 02:48.600
We're putting our practice time in the gym on the line.

02:49.350 --> 02:52.600
We want to train more and get better.

02:52.600 --> 02:54.930
Although we won the district tournament last year,

02:54.930 --> 02:56.610
we think we still have a lot to improve on.

02:56.610 --> 02:59.700
So we want more days to practise!

02:59.700 --> 03:02.610
But we were told it's impossible, because the girls' basketball club has to practise, too.

03:02.610 --> 03:05.370
Surely there's a way for both clubs to practise, right?

03:05.650 --> 03:08.500
Practising with those useless girls is just a waste of time!

03:09.280 --> 03:11.420
Here, here!

03:10.070 --> 03:11.420
Maho, here it comes!

03:15.250 --> 03:16.090
Ah, wait!

03:16.360 --> 03:17.510
Wait~

03:17.510 --> 03:18.090
Airin!

03:18.090 --> 03:19.460
Y-Yes!

03:20.350 --> 03:23.970
It's like they're just playing some children's game!

03:24.340 --> 03:26.850
That's why we consulted our advisor,

03:26.850 --> 03:29.480
but then he ended up having a fight with their advisor, Mihoshi.

03:30.000 --> 03:34.360
Before we knew it, it was decided that
we'd settle this with a basketball match.

03:34.360 --> 03:38.670
If the girls win, then everything will continue like it is now.

03:38.670 --> 03:40.820
If we win, we get to practise in the gym for six days a week,

03:40.820 --> 03:42.110
and the girls' basketball club will be dissolved.

03:42.740 --> 03:45.890
Well, it's obvious that'll happen,
since they're just playing around.

03:47.250 --> 03:49.670
It's great that you want to improve,

03:49.670 --> 03:52.370
but I don't think playing basketball just for fun is bad, either.

03:52.370 --> 03:52.870
But-

03:52.870 --> 03:54.830
As it stands, I'm just an outsider.

03:55.250 --> 03:57.650
I won't help either side.

03:57.650 --> 04:02.050
If you felt like it, you'd try to help the girls win, right?

04:02.050 --> 04:04.180
No matter what I do, three days just isn't enough time.

04:04.600 --> 04:06.130
I see.

04:06.130 --> 04:07.260
That's true.

04:07.260 --> 04:08.340
Hey, did you hear that?

04:08.340 --> 04:09.770
I was kind of scared; what a relief!

04:09.770 --> 04:11.520
Triangle, triangle!

04:11.950 --> 04:14.190
When you're feeling down, speak up!

04:15.600 --> 04:17.940
That's good, keep it up.

04:17.940 --> 04:18.570
Hinata!

04:18.840 --> 04:20.780
Oh~!

04:21.350 --> 04:24.660
We have to show Hasegawa-san our progress.

04:24.660 --> 04:27.500
We're going to get a lot better!

04:30.500 --> 04:32.030
What a relief!

04:32.030 --> 04:34.500
We thought you wouldn't be coming today.

04:34.500 --> 04:35.850
I'm sorry, Subaru.

04:35.850 --> 04:38.650
I apologise for yesterday.

04:38.650 --> 04:40.610
Um, Hasegawa-san...

04:40.610 --> 04:45.470
Although you only promised to coach us until today, if possible-

04:45.470 --> 04:47.600
You guys have a match, right?

04:47.960 --> 04:49.530
How did you know that?

04:49.530 --> 04:51.890
I heard it from the boys' basketball club.

04:51.890 --> 04:52.920
Then-

04:52.920 --> 04:53.620
I'm sorry.

04:53.620 --> 04:55.060
It's impossible.

04:55.500 --> 04:59.320
There's nothing I can do to ensure that you'll win.

04:59.950 --> 05:01.020
I'm sorry.

05:01.020 --> 05:02.490
There must be another way-

05:02.770 --> 05:04.450
There isn't another way!

05:04.450 --> 05:06.490
We don't have anyone other than...

05:06.490 --> 05:08.300
...anyone other than you!

05:08.300 --> 05:09.070
Help us!

05:11.650 --> 05:13.440
You're overestimating me.

05:13.440 --> 05:16.870
And also, I kind of understand the boys' feelings.

05:18.170 --> 05:19.810
That's mean...

05:19.810 --> 05:21.090
You're so mean!

05:21.550 --> 05:22.840
Maho!

05:25.530 --> 05:27.000
Hasegawa-san.

05:29.090 --> 05:32.650
We can still practise a little more, right?

05:32.650 --> 05:36.310
Please go ahead and coach us on your last day.

05:37.040 --> 05:38.850
Subaru's such a meanie!

05:39.250 --> 05:41.690
Saying things like, "I understand their feelings". I don't get him at all!

05:41.690 --> 05:44.540
Look, you're putting too much chilli powder on that!

05:44.540 --> 05:46.510
It's fine; I like it.

05:47.930 --> 05:52.690
But you know, what Hasegawa-san said is right, in a sense.

05:52.690 --> 05:55.600
He doesn't want to be irresponsible.

05:56.540 --> 05:57.580
That's-

05:57.580 --> 06:01.670
Even if today's his last day, is it really okay to just run out?

06:01.670 --> 06:02.340
I mean...

06:02.830 --> 06:06.020
Either way, since we're going to lose our coach,

06:06.020 --> 06:08.380
we'll have to think of something on our own.

06:11.010 --> 06:15.410
In the end, you were just using me to give those girls a glimmer of hope.

06:15.410 --> 06:18.350
Isn't it obvious that it's because they really want to win?

06:18.350 --> 06:19.290
It's impossible.

06:19.290 --> 06:21.770
I feel sorry for them. You're setting them up for a big let-down.

06:21.770 --> 06:24.730
If you think so, how about you continue, Coach?

06:24.730 --> 06:27.150
Those are different issues.

06:27.150 --> 06:30.070
I don't have that kind of passion.

06:31.600 --> 06:32.530
Don't run away.

06:32.530 --> 06:33.330
Huh?

06:33.330 --> 06:35.490
Don't run away from basketball.

06:35.950 --> 06:38.410
I'm not really running away.

06:38.410 --> 06:40.170
You "don't have the passion"?

06:40.170 --> 06:41.450
That's a lie.

06:41.450 --> 06:44.810
You didn't take up the job of coach because I blackmailed you into it.

06:44.810 --> 06:47.230
It was because you wanted to play basketball, even though you couldn't.

06:47.230 --> 06:49.670
You actually love it to a point where you can't control yourself.

06:49.670 --> 06:51.550
You tried to distance yourself from it, but it didn't work.

06:51.550 --> 06:53.350
That's just your delusion, Miho-nee!

06:53.350 --> 06:54.810
It's not a delusion.

06:54.810 --> 06:56.390
Subaru, you-

06:56.390 --> 06:58.060
You wouldn't understand, Miho-nee.

07:02.360 --> 07:03.720
Hey, Subaru.

07:03.720 --> 07:05.320
There was a girl you thought had promise, right?

07:05.730 --> 07:07.940
Are you just going to abandon her?

07:17.750 --> 07:20.110
That girl is too focused on winning.

07:20.110 --> 07:23.080
That girl just wants to stand out, right?

07:28.340 --> 07:29.970
Basketball is so amazing, isn't it?

07:29.970 --> 07:31.380
It's so cool!

07:31.380 --> 07:33.050
Would I be able to do it, too?

07:43.670 --> 07:46.070
Hey, Subaru!

07:46.070 --> 07:46.610
Huh?

07:46.610 --> 07:48.110
My, Mihoshi-chan.

07:48.770 --> 07:51.360
Subaru-kun said he was going out with some friends.

07:51.360 --> 07:53.320
Tch, he got away.

07:55.950 --> 07:57.220
Yo!

07:57.220 --> 07:58.120
Where's Aoi?

07:58.120 --> 08:00.870
Subaru, Kazunari!

08:06.520 --> 08:08.350
So, where shall we go?

08:08.350 --> 08:09.630
Anywhere's fine.

08:09.630 --> 08:13.220
You're as indifferent as usual, member of the lolicon club.

08:13.220 --> 08:14.260
Shut up.

08:14.600 --> 08:17.720
Then, how about we go to the batting centre?

08:17.720 --> 08:18.760
You'll feel refreshed!

08:18.760 --> 08:19.810
Oh, that sounds great.

08:19.810 --> 08:20.950
Let's go!

08:22.750 --> 08:24.270
It's pretty crowded.

08:24.270 --> 08:25.690
It's a holiday, after all.

08:25.690 --> 08:27.440
It looks like that's not the only reason.

08:27.440 --> 08:29.150
Free Throw Challenge

08:27.440 --> 08:29.150
10

08:27.440 --> 08:29.150
Make      free throws

08:27.440 --> 08:29.150
and get 1000 yen
worth of tickets free!

08:27.440 --> 08:29.150
Look at that.

08:29.510 --> 08:30.630
Want to do it?

08:30.630 --> 08:33.820
Do it yourself, Aoi, former member of the
Kirihara Middle School girls' basketball club.

08:33.820 --> 08:36.570
Subaru, are you afraid of losing to her?

08:36.570 --> 08:40.350
You're rusty because you've been slacking since the basketball club was suspended, right?

08:40.350 --> 08:43.730
You wouldn't want to let us seen how bad you've gotten, right?

08:46.210 --> 08:47.810
Harumotoya Ramen.

08:47.810 --> 08:49.800
Wontons and barbecued pork, large portions.

08:50.080 --> 08:52.090
<i>If</i>  you sink ten shots, that is!

09:02.680 --> 09:04.650
That's one successful shot!

09:03.500 --> 09:04.400
As expected.

09:04.400 --> 09:08.360
As usual, his form is so good that it irritates me.

09:13.220 --> 09:14.950
The second shot is successful!

09:16.500 --> 09:18.090
This isn't good...

09:18.090 --> 09:20.280
I've got to focus more...

09:31.600 --> 09:32.660
It's not enough...

09:32.660 --> 09:34.130
I've got to shoot more gently.

09:34.130 --> 09:35.130
More gently...

09:36.590 --> 09:37.430
My...

09:41.560 --> 09:42.560
My ideals are...

09:52.750 --> 09:54.190
Congratulations!

09:54.190 --> 09:56.150
You've pulled off ten successful shots!

09:58.520 --> 10:00.200
You really can do anything, Subaru.

10:00.680 --> 10:04.910
You weren't the runner-up in the prefecture tournament and the ace of Kirihara Middle school for nothing.

10:04.910 --> 10:07.620
Do you practise secretly?

10:08.790 --> 10:10.650
Subaru?

10:10.650 --> 10:11.710
Ah, no...

10:11.710 --> 10:16.310
Well, we've got the tickets, so let's go hit some balls!

10:18.740 --> 10:19.350
Sorry.

10:19.350 --> 10:20.970
I'm heading back for today.

10:23.530 --> 10:24.430
What was that?

10:24.430 --> 10:26.680
Maybe he has basketball withdrawal.

10:26.680 --> 10:27.770
Huh?

10:31.470 --> 10:34.610
I want to let those girls play basketball.

10:35.170 --> 10:37.900
The teacher in our school is such a sexist.

10:38.390 --> 10:41.700
He puts priority on the achievements of the boys' club over the "weak" girls' club.

10:41.700 --> 10:43.960
Supposedly it'll make the parents happy,

10:43.960 --> 10:45.880
and our enrolment will go up.

10:45.880 --> 10:48.080
Doesn't that just sound wrong?!

10:48.530 --> 10:50.500
Although they weren't very good when they started,

10:50.500 --> 10:53.500
no one has the right to take away their desire to play.

10:54.600 --> 10:56.770
Mihoshi-chan, you're making a teacher-like face.

10:56.770 --> 10:58.510
Well, I <i>am</i> a teacher, after all.

10:58.510 --> 10:59.920
Thanks for the meal.

10:59.920 --> 11:01.160
I'll come again.

11:01.160 --> 11:03.930
Onee-chan, could you try to help me convince Subaru?

11:04.400 --> 11:05.850
Okay!

11:13.610 --> 11:15.610
Hasegawa-san...

11:17.150 --> 11:18.380
Tomoka.

11:23.970 --> 11:26.510
Good afternoon.

11:26.510 --> 11:27.700
What a coincidence.

11:27.700 --> 11:30.080
Yeah.

11:30.530 --> 11:31.850
Going home after practice?

11:31.850 --> 11:36.080
No, I was going to practise on my own at school,

11:36.080 --> 11:39.030
but I couldn't use the gym because of the volleyball match.

11:39.030 --> 11:40.360
I see.

11:44.970 --> 11:46.400
See you, then.

11:46.400 --> 11:47.500
Yes!

11:47.500 --> 11:48.660
See you.

11:54.490 --> 11:55.610
Tomoka!

11:56.480 --> 11:57.830
Um...

11:57.830 --> 12:00.100
If it's okay with you, would you like to come to my house?

12:00.100 --> 12:01.990
There's a hoop there, at least.

12:03.000 --> 12:04.750
Is it fine with you?

12:04.750 --> 12:06.370
But, would I be troubling you?

12:06.750 --> 12:09.540
I have nothing more to teach you,

12:09.540 --> 12:11.040
but since we bumped into each other...

12:12.500 --> 12:14.830
Thank you very much!

12:21.910 --> 12:23.840
My heart is pounding.

12:23.840 --> 12:25.210
When we're riding a bike together,

12:25.210 --> 12:27.700
we're doing something bad.

12:27.700 --> 12:30.700
Sorry for making you do something bad.

12:32.400 --> 12:33.360
I see!

12:33.360 --> 12:35.310
She's Mihoshi-chan's student!

12:35.810 --> 12:37.520
My name is Minato Tomoka.

12:37.910 --> 12:42.580
I've been in Sensei and Hasegawa-san- Subaru-san's care.

12:43.350 --> 12:45.530
Mihoshi-chan was here until just a while ago...

12:45.530 --> 12:47.710
She'd just get in our way, so it's better that she's not here.

12:47.710 --> 12:50.580
Ah, Tomoka-chan, do you think you could stay for dinner?

12:50.580 --> 12:52.200
You don't need to trouble yourself.

12:52.200 --> 12:56.330
His father is away from home, so it's pretty lonely with just the two of us.

12:56.700 --> 12:58.090
Don't hold back!

12:58.090 --> 12:58.710
Okay?

12:59.850 --> 13:03.420
Mum, you'll be in the way of our practice, so could you go away?

13:03.420 --> 13:05.760
Okay.

13:05.760 --> 13:07.140
Then, take your time.

13:08.400 --> 13:09.690
Geez...

13:14.940 --> 13:17.400
This should be fine.

13:17.400 --> 13:20.480
I set it to the height of a mini-basketball hoop, so use it as much as you like.

13:22.400 --> 13:23.190
Um...!

13:25.490 --> 13:28.910
Please have a one-on-one match with me!

13:29.880 --> 13:33.290
If I win, please come back and coach us!

13:33.570 --> 13:34.710
Please!

13:38.430 --> 13:39.790
Okay.

13:39.790 --> 13:42.670
Then I'll be on defence, and you'll be on offence.

13:43.140 --> 13:44.840
I'm not allowed to jump.

13:44.840 --> 13:48.250
If you manage to score even once, I lose.

13:48.250 --> 13:48.840
How's that?

13:48.840 --> 13:51.050
I don't need a handicap!

13:51.050 --> 13:52.680
Having a handicap doesn't mean you're weak.

13:52.680 --> 13:55.160
It's there to balance out the game.

13:55.160 --> 13:55.730
But-

13:55.730 --> 13:57.640
For now, try getting one shot in.

14:04.010 --> 14:05.530
I'm ready when you are.

14:18.210 --> 14:19.000
She's fast.

14:28.630 --> 14:30.140
Amazing.

14:30.780 --> 14:33.150
Her dribbling doesn't look anything like an elementary schooler's dribbling.

14:33.150 --> 14:34.430
Her speed when she's moving back and forth...

14:38.310 --> 14:39.850
Is the jump shot coming?

14:45.620 --> 14:48.530
She's not going to jump because <i>I'm</i> not allowed to jump?

14:48.530 --> 14:49.740
Interesting.

14:55.980 --> 14:58.540
Your movement has gotten very sluggish.

14:58.540 --> 14:59.960
Isn't it about time you give up?

14:59.960 --> 15:01.060
No!

15:01.060 --> 15:03.250
We haven't reached the time limit!

15:03.250 --> 15:03.840
...Yet!

15:04.320 --> 15:05.750
So I won't give up!

15:14.390 --> 15:15.890
Sorry about that,

15:15.890 --> 15:19.050
but you wouldn't have liked it if I'd gone too easy on you.

15:19.050 --> 15:20.100
I understand...

15:20.100 --> 15:23.790
But I never thought you were this good.

15:23.790 --> 15:27.140
You'd probably do well even on teams outside of school.

15:27.140 --> 15:30.780
There's no meaning in playing basketball with a team other than the one I'm on now.

15:31.260 --> 15:33.200
Why are you so caught up on that?

15:33.200 --> 15:37.120
Everyone on that team is the reason why I can play basketball again.

15:38.540 --> 15:43.580
I wasn't a student of Keishin until the summer of last year.

15:43.960 --> 15:46.480
When it came to basketball, I became obsessed with winning,

15:46.480 --> 15:51.010
and couldn't satisfy myself until I had won.

15:51.980 --> 15:54.510
That's why I trained frantically every day,

15:54.510 --> 15:56.600
and I forced everyone to do the same.

15:57.650 --> 15:59.670
I became isolated.

15:59.670 --> 16:01.260
Of course that would have happened:

16:01.260 --> 16:04.900
I was so obsessed with winning and losing that I didn't consider the others' feelings.

16:06.730 --> 16:09.290
I couldn't bear to stay in that school, so I transferred.

16:10.490 --> 16:13.640
But I was still alone even after I transferred.

16:13.640 --> 16:17.100
I didn't know what to talk about with the people around me,

16:17.100 --> 16:18.660
but one day...

16:18.660 --> 16:20.200
You're saying too much, Natsuhi!

16:20.200 --> 16:21.300
Which part?!

16:21.300 --> 16:24.790
I just said that if she sucks, and yet she still tries to shoot, she's just being a bother!

16:24.790 --> 16:27.630
It's weird to say that only the good players should shoot!

16:27.630 --> 16:29.240
What part of that is weird?

16:29.240 --> 16:31.170
I'll settle this with you today, once and for all!

16:31.170 --> 16:33.050
That's my line!

16:33.050 --> 16:34.470
Oh, that's great.

16:34.810 --> 16:37.420
Since you're at it, why don't we make it a girls-against-boys match?

16:37.420 --> 16:39.260
Exactly what we want!

16:39.260 --> 16:40.850
Tomoka, you'll take part too, right?

16:41.890 --> 16:43.520
Me?

16:43.850 --> 16:45.940
It's okay to go all out.

16:54.310 --> 16:56.780
In the end, my old habit kicked in.

16:56.780 --> 16:59.160
I did everything myself, and we won the match.

17:00.180 --> 17:03.520
And then, when I thought that everyone would leave me again...

17:03.520 --> 17:06.100
Basketball is so amazing, isn't it?

17:06.100 --> 17:07.580
It's so cool!

17:07.580 --> 17:09.460
Would I be able to do it, too?

17:09.460 --> 17:11.420
Teach me, Mo-kan!

17:12.120 --> 17:15.780
And in the end, we decided to make a basketball club.

17:15.780 --> 17:18.550
Then Maho invited her childhood friend, Saki.

17:19.150 --> 17:22.310
Although she wasn't interested at first,

17:23.560 --> 17:25.690
Maho managed to convince her.

17:28.630 --> 17:32.480
Soon after, Airi and Hinata joined, too.

17:32.480 --> 17:34.990
And so, it became the girls' basketball club.

17:35.490 --> 17:36.730
I see.

17:36.730 --> 17:44.430
I thought the bad me would appear again, but it was very fun.

17:44.430 --> 17:48.120
Everyone taught me that you can play basketball just for fun.

17:48.540 --> 17:52.590
That there's something more important than just winning and losing.

17:53.510 --> 17:58.330
I don't want to become too obsessed with winning and have it lose that important place.

17:58.330 --> 17:59.940
That's all I want.

17:59.940 --> 18:02.770
If you lose the match, what will you do?

18:04.080 --> 18:05.890
I will quit basketball.

18:05.890 --> 18:08.350
I will never play basketball again.

18:08.350 --> 18:12.050
Even if I don't play basketball, as long as I can be with everyone...

18:12.050 --> 18:14.570
Are you going to lie and deny your love for basketball?

18:14.570 --> 18:16.110
It's not a lie.

18:16.410 --> 18:17.910
I like basketball.

18:17.910 --> 18:22.030
But the most important thing to me is that the five of us can be together.

18:23.990 --> 18:28.620
And I'm happy that I managed to see Subaru-san one last time.

18:29.370 --> 18:32.250
I'm sorry for being so much trouble. You even let me shower here...

18:32.250 --> 18:34.560
Are you sure you don't want me to come with you to the train station?

18:34.560 --> 18:36.300
Yes, it's fine.

18:36.570 --> 18:38.220
Then, goodbye.

18:49.800 --> 18:51.650
Hey, Subaru-kun.

18:51.650 --> 18:52.150
Dinner-

18:52.150 --> 18:53.410
Mum.

18:53.410 --> 18:55.860
I'll be going out for a moment.

18:55.860 --> 18:56.570
As for dinner,

18:56.870 --> 18:58.240
make it for three people.

19:06.750 --> 19:07.650
Tomoka!

19:09.060 --> 19:10.990
Subaru-san...

19:10.990 --> 19:11.920
Don't quit.

19:13.500 --> 19:16.390
I thought I had no passion.

19:16.390 --> 19:17.550
But that's impossible.

19:17.850 --> 19:18.720
It's impossible.

19:19.510 --> 19:21.630
I can't let you go!

19:24.070 --> 19:26.100
You can't quit basketball!

19:26.530 --> 19:28.860
If there's only one place where you can play basketball,

19:28.860 --> 19:30.700
you shouldn't let go of it.

19:32.020 --> 19:33.890
Hey, please!

19:33.890 --> 19:39.300
You shoot so beautifully. Please don't say you're quitting so easily!

19:40.800 --> 19:43.700
I didn't say it easily.

19:45.220 --> 19:46.990
I don't want to quit.

19:48.110 --> 19:49.660
I really...

19:49.660 --> 19:51.330
I really don't want to quit!

19:51.330 --> 19:52.290
Then don't!

19:52.290 --> 19:52.870
But-

19:52.870 --> 19:53.670
I'll protect it.

19:55.090 --> 19:57.130
I'll protect both of them.

19:57.450 --> 19:59.590
Your basketball, and the place where you all belong...

19:59.590 --> 20:00.920
I will protect them.

20:01.450 --> 20:03.020
I want you to let me protect them.

20:04.960 --> 20:06.210
But...

20:06.210 --> 20:07.600
...you said we couldn't win.

20:08.010 --> 20:11.350
Frankly, there's not much chance of winning yet,

20:11.350 --> 20:15.310
but I'll do anything to protect your basketball!

20:27.330 --> 20:28.900
Subaru-san...

20:37.580 --> 20:38.800
Yes!

20:40.960 --> 20:42.150
What is it?

20:42.150 --> 20:43.260
I need some information.

20:43.580 --> 20:44.680
Anything is fine.

20:44.680 --> 20:46.340
Do you have any data on the boys' basketball club?

20:50.010 --> 20:53.270
I knew you were gonna ask me this sooner or later, so I prepared it.

20:53.270 --> 20:54.550
Thank you.

20:54.550 --> 20:55.730
See you.

20:56.660 --> 20:57.650
Hey, Subaru.

20:58.000 --> 20:59.350
Do you think they can win?

20:59.350 --> 21:02.600
Well, normally, it would be impossible.

21:02.600 --> 21:06.950
But wouldn't it be fun to change the impossible into the possible?

21:10.090 --> 21:11.800
Welcome back, Subaru.

21:14.100 --> 21:15.460
I did it, everyone!

21:15.460 --> 21:17.500
Subaru-san said he'll coach us!

21:17.500 --> 21:18.250
Really?

21:18.250 --> 21:19.400
Thank goodness.

21:19.400 --> 21:20.550
Oh~

21:20.550 --> 21:22.380
Onii-chan, welcome back!

21:22.380 --> 21:26.630
Well, I always knew that Subarun would never betray us.

21:26.630 --> 21:28.240
Oh?

21:28.240 --> 21:30.880
But, that aside, "Subaru-san", huh?

21:30.880 --> 21:31.400
Huh?

21:31.400 --> 21:34.480
Subaru will make us work hard!

21:41.410 --> 21:43.610
Damn, just worrying won't accomplish anything.

21:43.610 --> 21:45.820
Let's get this over with and apologise.

21:46.280 --> 21:49.120
Welcome back, Master!

22:00.960 --> 22:03.510
I want to grow up quickly (Yes-!)

22:13.220 --> 22:14.560
Come on! Come on!

22:14.560 --> 22:17.310
If I'm small, if I stay small

22:17.310 --> 22:19.810
You say there's virtue in it.

22:19.810 --> 22:21.400
But that's a lie!

22:21.400 --> 22:22.480
You're just trying to console me, right?

22:22.770 --> 22:25.110
I want to grow up faster!

22:25.530 --> 22:28.200
Drink milk, drink soy milk

22:28.200 --> 22:30.910
You say that the shrimp there is good.

22:30.910 --> 22:32.280
Triple A

22:32.280 --> 22:34.160
I don't need any ratings

22:34.160 --> 22:36.160
I want to grow up faster!

22:36.160 --> 22:36.960
Dribble!

22:36.960 --> 22:37.620
Zig-zag

22:37.620 --> 22:38.290
Defence!

22:38.290 --> 22:39.170
Offence (Yep!)

22:39.170 --> 22:41.250
I want to shoot the ball

22:42.000 --> 22:49.300
I want to be praised soon... by you

22:49.840 --> 22:52.350
"Look here. Look here. It's going to end!"

22:52.350 --> 22:55.010
Jump! Jump!

22:55.310 --> 22:57.520
More and more and more

22:58.390 --> 23:03.230
When can I become an adult

23:03.230 --> 23:09.030
I'm growing! It's painful! The painful sores.

23:09.320 --> 23:13.830
However, I'll definitely show you that I can endure it

23:13.830 --> 23:21.040
Shake, Bounce, Touch, Aim for the goal!

23:21.420 --> 23:24.500
Ah! I want to grow up faster!

23:25.710 --> 23:29.280
Um, in next week's episode, Hinata will be carried by Subaru-san,

23:29.280 --> 23:31.640
and Kamokiri-sensei will have a fight with Mihoshi-sensei-

23:31.640 --> 23:32.890
What kind of episode is that?

23:32.890 --> 23:34.030
Well, it's-

23:34.030 --> 23:34.500
Tomo!

23:34.500 --> 23:35.940
The time, the time!

23:35.940 --> 23:37.520
And so, see you next week!

23:37.020 --> 23:40.020
Next Time:

23:37.020 --> 23:40.020
The Pass That Leads to Tomorrow

23:37.520 --> 23:40.020
In the end, what <i>is</i> it about?
